<?php declare(strict_types=1);require_once __DIR__.'/includes/header.php';?><main><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Legal</div><h1>Privacy policy.</h1><p>Clear information about local account data and download activity.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container article"><div class="article-body"><p>2B2X Browser stores account, download, support, and contact records on its local server. These records are used to provide account features, serve downloads, and respond to support requests.</p><h2>Local storage</h2><p>JSON files are stored in the project’s data directory. Passwords are hashed with PHP’s password hashing system and are never stored as plain text.</p><h2>Download records</h2><p>Download records include the release, operating system, architecture, timestamp, and a one-way IP hash. An IP hash is not a reversible identifier and is used only for basic activity context.</p><h2>Data control</h2><p>Users can view their download history and may request account deletion through the support channel. Administrators retain records needed for transparency, security, and service integrity.</p><h2>Security</h2><p>Sessions use HTTP-only cookies, CSRF protection, rate-limiting is recommended for public forms, and production deployments should use HTTPS with a trusted certificate.</p></div></div></section></main><?php require_once __DIR__.'/includes/footer.php'; ?>
